  ;; One step of the Gaborish inverse (photo-xyb.mjs gaborishStep) over a plane of W x H f64 samples at `p`, its original
  ;; at `orig` and two rows of scratch at `ring`: G's row y into the ring, then row y - 1 updated by p += orig - G p; the
  ;; window repeats the edge sample past each edge. Every sum is the JavaScript's, in its order:
  ;; (mc + w1 * (((uc + dc) + ml) + mr) + w2 * (((ul + ur) + dl) + dr)) * norm. Two samples a lane pair inside the row,
  ;; the first and last samples alone. W is even and at least 4.
  (func (export "gab") (param $p i32) (param $orig i32) (param $ring i32) (param $W i32) (param $H i32)
    (param $w1 f64) (param $w2 f64) (param $norm f64)
    (local $y i32) (local $row i32) (local $u i32) (local $m i32) (local $d i32) (local $o i32) (local $x i32) (local $end i32)
